pub fn html()->String{r#"<div class="modal-shade"><section class="report-modal legal-modal" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="report-title"><button class="close-modal" data-action="close" aria-label="Close terms and privacy">×</button><p class="kicker">UNIVERSAL FRAME · UPDATED OCTOBER 5, 2026</p><h2 id="report-title" tabindex="-1">Terms &amp; privacy</h2><p class="legal-emphasis"><strong>For design exploration and preliminary estimating only.</strong> This studio helps you visualize concepts. It does not provide licensed architecture, engineering, surveying, legal advice, an approved building plan or authorization to construct.</p><h3>Your design and professional review</h3><p>Dimensions, framing geometry, layouts, materials, prices, code profiles and screening results may contain omissions or errors. Historical reference plans and generated designs are not certified for modern construction. Verify every output with a qualified architect, structural engineer, licensed contractor and the permitting authority for the actual site. Site conditions, loads, foundations, accessibility, egress, fire safety, utilities, product specifications and local amendments require independent review. Do not rely on this tool to decide whether a structure is safe.</p><p>Reports are preliminary review packages. ForteWEB analysis has not run in this version. Third-party references and preliminary span tables do not constitute third-party approval. Universal Frame is not affiliated with or endorsed by Weyerhaeuser, Huber or any code authority. Their names and marks belong to their respective owners.</p><h3>Estimates and purchases</h3><p>Prices are editable sample budget rates, not quotations, offers or guaranteed totals. Quantities represent the model, not a complete procurement list. Waste, delivery, sitework, engineering, taxes, approvals and other project costs may differ or be excluded. Verify suppliers, product suitability, measurements and complete project costs before ordering or buying.</p><h3>No warranties; limits on liability</h3><p><strong>TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT PERMITTED BY APPLICABLE LAW, THIS TOOL AND ITS OUTPUTS ARE PROVIDED “AS IS” AND “AS AVAILABLE,” WITHOUT EXPRESS OR IMPLIED WARRANTIES, INCLUDING MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE, ACCURACY, AVAILABILITY OR NON-INFRINGEMENT.</strong></p><p>To the extent permitted by applicable law, Universal Frame and its operators are not liable for loss or damage arising from use of, inability to use, or reliance on the tool or its outputs, including construction defects, purchasing decisions, lost data, lost profits or consequential losses. You are responsible for independent verification and for the decisions you make.</p><p>These provisions do not exclude liability or waive consumer rights that cannot lawfully be excluded, including any liability for intentional misconduct, gross negligence or other matters protected by applicable law. Some jurisdictions do not allow particular warranty exclusions or liability limitations; the affected provisions apply only to the extent allowed. Nothing here promises that a disclaimer eliminates all liability. If a provision is unenforceable, the remaining provisions continue to the extent permitted.</p><h3>Privacy and your files</h3><p>House calculations and edits run in your browser. This version has no studio signup, application account, advertising trackers or analytics. Designs are not automatically saved to an application server; download your design JSON and reports before leaving. The hosting provider may process normal technical request information to deliver and protect the website.</p><p>When you request a ZIP lookup, your ZIP code is sent to Zippopotam.us, which also receives ordinary connection information such as your IP address. You can instead select a state and county. Exported reports may include the project name or address you enter; you control who receives those files. Opening third-party links subjects you to those sites’ own terms and privacy practices.</p><h3>Use and attribution</h3><p>Use the tool lawfully. Do not disrupt it, attempt unauthorized access or present preliminary outputs as approved plans. Reference scans, furniture, textures and other assets retain their stated licenses and attribution requirements. The Asset credits links and source package list the relevant notices. Keep a copy of the terms displayed when generating your report.</p><p class="muted">The studio is a concept tool; a professional review remains part of every real building project.</p><button class="button primary wide" data-action="close">Back to my design</button></section></div>"#.into()}
